<title>HUNGARY: SOCCER-OLYMPIQUE NIMES GO THROUGH IN BUDAPEST.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-OLYMPIQUE NIMES GO THROUGH IN BUDAPEST.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olympique Nimes of France beat Kispest Honved of Hungary 2-1 (2-0) in the second leg of their first round European Cup Winners' Cup tie played on Thursday in Budapest.</p>
<p>Nimes go through 5-2 on aggregate and are the first third division club ever to win through a round of a European Cup competition.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Kispest Honved:</p>
<p>Attila Piroska (62nd)</p>
<p>Olympique Nimes:</p>
<p>Ecker (6th), Sabin (39th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
